<title>INDONESIA: Unibank says no problem with liquidity.</title>
<headline>Unibank says no problem with liquidity.</headline>
<dateline>JAKARTA 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indonesia's medium-sized bank, PT United City Bank (Unibank), said on Friday it had not suffered from tight liquidity in the money market, bank officials said.</p>
<p>&quot;We have no problem with liquidity,&quot; said one bank official.</p>
<p>The bank said in a statement it was a net lender as of August 14, when it placed 236.725 billion rupiah to the non-bank and interbank markets, while its borrowings were nil.</p>
